# Target C-II — slack-aware one-anchor component count

**Date:** 2026-09-18  
**Status:** conditional proved candidate; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** the degree-pure one-anchor decomposition after the promoted support-five exclusion and the proof-only noncollapsed support-six exclusions  
**Dependencies:** support-five `K_5` exclusion; uniform and simple-wall support-six `H5` projection-potential exclusions; audited train-closure host deficiency; disjoint-support one-anchor component decomposition  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_one_anchor_slack_aware_component_count_2026_09_18.py`

This is the first exact propagation of the new support-six work into the component
count. It does not claim the full C-II closure or promote theorem state.

## Statement

Let `m` be the number of degree-pure one-anchor relation components in the
decomposition to which the existing support-five/support-six route applies, and let
`n_1` be the number of one-anchor faces in those components. Let `m_6` be the number
of support-six components. Then

\[
\boxed{7m\le n_1+s_Z.}
\tag{1}
\]

Equivalently,

\[
\boxed{m\le {n_1+s_Z\over7}.}
\tag{2}
\]

In the exact zero-slack sector this becomes `m<=n_1/7`.

## Proof

The support-five `K_5` endpoint is excluded by the existing reciprocal theorem. The
new projection-potential certificates exclude every noncollapsed support-six `H5`
representative, including all six uniform and all ten simple-wall orbits. The prior
`H7/H6` exclusions and the double-wall theorem cover the other noncollapsed
support-six strata. Hence every surviving degree-pure component either:

1. has support at least seven; or
2. has support six and is collapsed, with all six outer anchors projectively parallel.

For each collapsed support-six component, the host graph is connected and the exact
host-transpose calculation gives a one-dimensional kernel. The audited host-deficiency
identity embeds these row-dual spaces with disjoint support into the global pure-contact
stress space, so

\[
 m_6\le \sigma_C\le s_Z.
\tag{3}
\]

The face population obeys

\[
 n_1\ge 6m_6+7(m-m_6)=7m-m_6.
\tag{4}
\]

Combining (3) and (4) gives (1).

The argument is exact and does not treat the two-dimensional local collapsed angle
family as a global source realization. It charges only the global host-kernel
deficiency supplied by the audited train-closure framework.

## Canonical-quantity propagation

The exact canonical quantity improved here is the number `m` of one-anchor relation
components in the degree-pure closure count. Any downstream rank/corank inequality
that previously inserted the coarse bound `m<=n_1/6` may, within this scope, insert

\[
 m\le(n_1+s_Z)/7.
\]

The `s_Z/7` correction must be retained; silently replacing it by `n_1/7` at positive
slack would be invalid. In the zero-slack branch the support-six collapsed endpoint
is absent and the sharp coefficient is `n_1/7`.

This does not yet close the global Target C-II inequalities because the canonical
frontier allows arbitrary `s_Z>=0`. The remaining smallest obstruction is a positive-
slack collapsed component, together with whatever global diameter/bar constraints are
needed to eliminate it.

**Disposition:** conditional proved candidate; exact slack-aware support count; C-II
remains open and theorem-state authority is unchanged.
